{"schema":"mao-cross-channel-public-site-data/1","script":"CCC0031c.dsf","adjudicated":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:800503","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccc0031c:00001","script":"CCC0031c.dsf","ordinal":1,"jp":"桜庭がいた。","en":"There was Sakuraba,","comments":[],"refs":["ccfc:sn:0207:0000011b:text"],"binding":"resolved","verdict":"acceptable","severity":"style","confidence":"high","categories":["presentation"],"assessment":"The English is supportable by the bound Japanese source in this unit.","remedy":"","highlights":[]},{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:800504","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccc0031c:00002","script":"CCC0031c.dsf","ordinal":2,"jp":"ベッドに寝ていた。","en":"sleeping in a bed.","comments":["See CCA0016... but first, see CCC0025. That script touched on something of Yusa, who has more than a few parallels with Misato, as well as the hexagon thing that will return in the Misato Sendback scene. Him being asleep in the infirmary should be taken to be the reading key for the same scene in Week 1. Unfortunately, I think CCB0005 works much better, but I suppose further evidence is always good. -GHS"],"refs":["ccfc:sn:0207:0000013f:text"],"binding":"resolved","verdict":"acceptable","severity":"style","confidence":"high","categories":["presentation"],"assessment":"The English is supportable by the bound Japanese source in this unit.","remedy":"","highlights":[]},{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:800505","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccc0031c:00003","script":"CCC0031c.dsf","ordinal":3,"jp":"腹を出して、爆睡している。","en":"Belly out, fast asleep.","comments":[],"refs":["ccfc:sn:0207:00000169:text"],"binding":"resolved","verdict":"acceptable","severity":"style","confidence":"high","categories":["presentation"],"assessment":"The English is supportable by the bound Japanese source in this unit.","remedy":"","highlights":[]},{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:800506","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccc0031c:00004","script":"CCC0031c.dsf","ordinal":4,"jp":"「……ぐおー」","en":"Sakuraba: \"...snooooooore.\"","comments":["\"Snore\". First a sound, contrast Misato's sobbing... -GHS"],"refs":